  "name": null,
  "problem": "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $⟨ia,b⟩=i⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n\nII. $⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=⟨\\alpha a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n\nIII. $⟨ia,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$",
